      "headline": "Germany signals Bundeswehr participation in Strait of Hormus naval mission; German Navy begins planning",
      "summary": "Following a Paris conference of roughly 30 states convened by France and the UK on 18 April, Chancellor Merz signalled Germany would offer minehunting vessels and maritime patrol aircraft for a potential international mission to reopen the Strait of Hormus, which Iran has blockaded since the outbreak of the Iran war. Defence Minister Pistorius confirmed the Bundeswehr has begun concrete mission planning, while stipulating conditions including a ceasefire, a UN mandate, and US participation. By 19 April Iran had partially re-opened then re-closed the strait, keeping Germany's possible contribution in flux.",
