      "headline": "Iran war energy shock: Germany debates kerosene shortage, National Security Council convened, fuel subsidies enacted",
      "summary": "The Iran war's blockade of the Strait of Hormus triggered warnings of an imminent kerosene shortage in Germany by May, with Finance Minister Klingbeil urging urgent preparations while Economics Minister Reiche downplayed risks and opposed a fuel transition levy. Chancellor Merz announced he would convene the newly created National Security Council 'soon' to address energy security, while the coalition enacted a two-month fuel tax cut of 17 cents per litre. The IMF cut Germany's 2026 growth forecast to 0.8%, and Klingbeil said Germany was feeling the Iran war's economic effects directly.",
